  "answer": "I'll look through how special prices are applied on the storefront and compare that with the admin API path that sets start and end dates.The admin save path looks suspicious around special dates. I'll trace how the storefront decides a special is active before changing anything.The storefront price check and the admin save path both look wrong for dated specials. I'll add a failing test that covers an end date with and without a start date, then fix whatever that test shows.A special with only an end date is priced correctly once the dates are stored in the right fields. A start and an end together never qualify, and the admin mapper writes the end date into the start field. I'll fix both.Dated specials never reached the storefront because the admin product mapper saved the discount end date in the special start-date field, and the catalogue price calculation then required that same start date to be both before and after today. The mapper now stores the end date on the end-date field, and the price calculation treats a special as active when the start date is already past and the end date is still ahead. Specials with no dates are unchanged. Products already saved with the end date in the start field need to be saved again.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialPriceTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\", \"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialPriceTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"storefront HTTP response for a product created through the admin REST API\"], \"missing\": [\"a running shop with an admin API fixture that creates a product special and reads it back from the storefront\"]}",
